"[ImageFetcher] Do not follow symlinks in ImageDataStoreDisk" (crbug
574604188; no CVE listed yet): the image cache read and wrote entries
following symlinks, so a symlink planted in the cache directory made the
browser process read or overwrite files outside it (on Mac, where a less
privileged process can write there; on Linux the cache is in the profile:
defence in depth). chromium/src main commit
8a3b03133f6c8b3b857b3e9942e2caeebda8fc09 (main@{#1730706}), merged on
2026-10-30 to 157 as bbcb710241054370f1d70ef03bf104058d081db8
(refs/branch-heads/8103@{#997}, after the 157.0.8103.33 tag); the 156 merge
(Gerrit CL 8687489) was still open. This is the 157 merge, without its test.
Drop it once a 157 tag has it.

